  "raw": " seven months, and a rental dispute may be the reason why the organisation quits the country.\n\nJeff Spiteri, head of Cardiff Aviation, founded in 2004, told councillors that the company had been “bound and determined” to cover both the airtaxi and floating building rent bill that was due on July 1.\n\n“We were bound and determined to cover the bills ... but there is a difference [between] being bound and being positive. It is not the negotiation that would be productive,” he said.\n\n“We have spoken to the landlord, we have spoken to the relevant councillors ... we spoke formally to them for a seven month cut off and none of them spoke to us over a seven month period.”\n\nSpiteri said he owed “six figures” in rent because the negotiations moved back and forth consistently for several years. He claimed that Legacy Aviation, which is under pressure to decide whether to allow Cardiff",
